# ============================================================================
# Cloud Operations Agent - environment configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Everything has a sane local default, so an empty
# .env (or none at all) runs the full stack in mock mode on localhost.
#
# Precedence for all services: environment variable > config/*.yaml > default.
# Secrets belong ONLY here (or a real secret store), never in config/*.yaml,
# which is committed to git and hot-reloaded into running services.
# ============================================================================

# --- Global -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory holding the hot-reloadable configuration tree (prompts, checks,
# fleet registry, gateway server registry). Relative paths resolve from the
# repo root.
CLOUDOPS_CONFIG_DIR=./config

# dev | prod. In dev the services log pretty console lines; in prod they log
# single-line JSON for log shippers.
CLOUDOPS_ENV=dev

# debug | info | warning | error
CLOUDOPS_LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Inference (Ollama) -----------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the Ollama server used by the agent through LiteLLM.
# The model name itself lives in config/models.yaml (hot-reloadable).
OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434

# --- Service ports ----------------------------------------------------------
CLOUDOPS_AGENT_PORT=8001
CLOUDOPS_GATEWAY_PORT=8010
CLOUDOPS_MCP_OPENSHIFT_PORT=8011
CLOUDOPS_MCP_OBSERVABILITY_PORT=8012
CLOUDOPS_MCP_REGISTRY_PORT=8013
CLOUDOPS_BFF_PORT=8080

# URL the agent uses to reach the MCP gateway.
CLOUDOPS_GATEWAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8010/mcp

# URL the BFF uses to reach the agent's A2A endpoint.
CLOUDOPS_AGENT_A2A_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001

# --- Fleet registry (MongoDB) -----------------------------------------------
# The registry service's store: applications, clusters, placements, and the
# credentials each cluster is reached with. This is the one part of the stack
# that holds STATE rather than configuration, which is why it is a database
# and not a file under config/.
#
# `make mongo-up` runs mongo:8 as container cloudops-mongo bound to loopback;
# `make mongo-seed` loads config/fleet/*.yaml into it idempotently.
#
# A deployed instance puts its credentials in the URL below, where they stay
# out of the committed, hot-reloaded config tree (FR-CFG-4), e.g.
#   CLOUDOPS_MONGO_URL=mongodb://cloudops:<password>@mongo.example.internal:27017/?tls=true
CLOUDOPS_MONGO_URL=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
CLOUDOPS_MONGO_DB=cloudops

# --- MCP server backends ----------------------------------------------------
# mock: serve deterministic synthetic fleet data (no cluster access needed).
# live: talk to real OpenShift API servers and Prometheus/Thanos.
CLOUDOPS_BACKEND_MODE=mock

# Live mode only. Both live backends authenticate from the kubeconfig on disk
# (first KUBECONFIG entry, else ~/.kube/config) using the context each cluster
# names under the `live:` section of config/fleet/fleet.yaml, so credentials
# never live in the committed config tree. See the README section
# "Live mode against a local kind fleet".
# KUBECONFIG=

# Live mode only, for a fleet that fronts its clusters with a shared
# Prometheus/Thanos endpoint instead of one Prometheus per cluster. The local
# kind fleet needs neither: each cluster's Prometheus is reached through the
# API server's service proxy with the same kubeconfig identity.
# CLOUDOPS_OCP_TOKEN=
# CLOUDOPS_THANOS_URL=https://thanos-querier.example.com
# CLOUDOPS_THANOS_TOKEN=

# --- OpenTelemetry ----------------------------------------------------------
# When set, every service exports OTLP traces (and logs where supported) to
# this endpoint, e.g. the collector from deploy/docker-compose.yaml.
# When unset, tracing still runs in-process (trace ids appear in logs) but
# nothing is exported, so the stack works with zero extra infrastructure.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# --- Authentication mode (PRD D5, FR-ID-2/3) -------------------------------
# dev  (default): the console shows a persona picker backed by
#                 config/identity/users.yaml; no tokens involved.
# oidc:           every chat request must carry Authorization: Bearer <JWT>,
#                 verified against the JWKS + issuer + audience below and
#                 mapped to the same claim shape the picker produces.
CLOUDOPS_AUTH_MODE=dev
# CLOUDOPS_OIDC_ISSUER=https://idp.example.com/realms/cloudops
# CLOUDOPS_OIDC_AUDIENCE=cloudops-console
# CLOUDOPS_OIDC_JWKS_URL=https://idp.example.com/realms/cloudops/protocol/openid-connect/certs
# Inline JWKS JSON (tests / air-gapped; wins over the URL when set):
# CLOUDOPS_OIDC_JWKS={"keys":[...]}
# Claim carrying group membership (array or space/comma string):
# CLOUDOPS_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups
